# Rust. Nothing here builds it any more -- the engine and the Rust SDK are their
# own repositories and carry their own rules -- but a sibling checkout made
# inside this tree by mistake should still not be committed.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Go
go/bin/
*.test
*.out

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Apple
.DS_Store
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
*.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/IDEWorkspaceChecks.plist
Pods/

# Swift build output. The Swift SDK and its sample now live in moqom-swift,
# which carries its own rules for these; kept here because a stray checkout or
# a scratch package under this tree should still not be committed.
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj/

# Terraform. State is in GCS and never on disk; a *.tfstate here means someone
# ran a root without initialising its backend, and it will contain credentials.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
!*.tfvars.json.example
backend.hcl
!backend.hcl.example

# Root lock files are committed on purpose. They pin the exact provider builds
# and their checksums, so CI and a laptop resolve to the same code and a
# compromised registry release cannot be substituted silently. Regenerate with
# `terraform providers lock` for every platform that runs Terraform, not just
# your own — a lock file missing linux_amd64 breaks CI and looks like a network
# error when it does.
#
# Module lock files are ignored, and the asymmetry is deliberate. A module is
# never applied on its own; the only thing that initialises one is CI running
# `validate` against it. Such a run writes a lock file for whichever platform
# happened to produce it, and committing that single-platform file is strictly
# worse than having none: the next machine with a different OS fails init on a
# checksum mismatch. The pinning that matters already lives in the roots.
deploy/modules/*/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
service-account*.json

# Editors
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Build artifacts
*.xcframework
*.aar
*.wasm
pkg/

# Local scratch
/tmp/
/scratch/
